        "original_id": "0c4d38fe-5e7e-543a-a549-9fbaaec55e8a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 1974 South African Grand Prix\n- Places: Kyalami, Midrand, Gauteng province, South Africa\n- Products: BRM P201\n- People: Jean-Pierre Beltoise\n- Topics: Formula One, motor racing circuits\n\nFacts:\n- The 1974 South African Grand Prix was a Formula One motor race held at Kyalami on 30 March 1974.\n- Kyalami Racing Circuit is a motor racing circuit in Midrand, Gauteng province, South Africa.\n- Kyalami Racing Circuit takes its name from the Zulu phrase \"Khaya lami,\" meaning \"My home.\"\n- The BRM P201 achieved its best finish on its debut when Jean-Pierre Beltoise placed second at the 1974 South African Grand Prix.",
